  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Issue Identified**: ChatSidebar component was rendering child tasks twice - once in normal expanded mode and once in compact mode.\n\n2. **Root Cause**: Both `v-if=\"!isCompact\"` and `v-else` blocks were rendering the same `rootChildren` array without proper conditional wrapping.\n\n3. **Solution Applied**: Wrapped entire hierarchy tree section in a parent `<template v-if=\"rootChildren.length\">` to ensure normal and compact modes are mutually exclusive.\n\n4. **Key Change**: Normal mode shows full list, compact mode shows icon list - only one renders at a time based on `isCompact` state.\n\n5. **Result**: Eliminated duplicate child task rendering while maintaining both UI modes functionality.",
